\title{tncensus: Tunisian Census Data (1891-2024 Censuses and Harmonized Panel)}
\description{
\if{html}{\figure{logo.png}{options: style='float: right' alt='logo' width='120'}}

Comprehensive R data package for Tunisia's population censuses from 1891 to 2024. Combines (1) the harmonized 2014-2024 delegation-level panel (281 delegations, 45 indicators, crosswalk, and codebook); (2) full 2014 RGPH data (264 delegations, 169 variables, and 28 disaggregated tables); (3) full 2024 RGPH data (279 delegations, 24 governorates, national totals, 46 thematic indicators, optional secteur-level download, accessors, and Gini/Theil inequality functions); (4) 2004 RGPH data (264 delegations, 24 governorates, national totals, 48 indicators); (5) 1984 RGPH delegation-level education tables and 1966 governorate illiteracy data; (6) historical national education series (1956-2014) and master INS delegation crosswalk; (7) colonial-era population censuses (1891-1956); and (8) 199 tables transcribed from the 1906 European and 1931 indigenous census publications and from the demography, health and public-instruction chapters of the Statistique generale de la Tunisie yearbooks (1921-1936 census tables and 1902-1939 vital, migration, naturalisation, hospital, mortality, public-assistance and school-enrolment series), digitized on Gallica (Bibliotheque nationale de France). Original contemporary data published by INS Tunisia \url{https://www.ins.tn/}.
}
